    "narrative": "The LawDog offensive unit faces a favorable slate today, led by **Jonathan Aranda**, whose 70.47 score makes him our clear anchor. **Jonathan Aranda** benefits from a high-leverage matchup against Bieber (5.10 xERA), with the combination of a positive park factor and a premium spot in the two-hole yielding a massive 19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s inefficiency. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a high-floor start at 65.73; while the matchup against Bradley is slightly tougher, his elite dynamic platoon profile and the aggressive base-stealing potential against a slow-to-the-plate starter keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier. **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Gleyber Torres** round out our top-tier exposure, both benefiting from ideal order placement, though **Gleyber Torres** faces a slight drag due to his platoon splits against Dobnak.\n\nOur most difficult decision at the margins was relegating **Gavin Sheets** to the bench with a 35.12 score. While **Gavin Sheets** typically provides a dependable power floor, he fell below our 40.0 \"Zebras\" threshold due to a brutal matchup against Sale (3.14 xERA). The negative 19% adjustment for the pitcher's elite skill level effectively neutralized his park and recency advantages. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of **Will Smith**, who remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on our active core of **Masyn Winn** and **Ryan Waldschmidt** to fill the gaps. **Masyn Winn** remains a vital piece of our strategy, as his 86% sprint efficiency against Pfaadt provides the scarcity-driven value we need to maintain our pace in the SB category, despite a slight park penalty. We have no significant weather risks to report, but owners should keep a close eye on the late-afternoon lineups for **Ryan Waldschmidt**, as his position at the bottom of the order leaves him the most vulnerable to a defensive replacement if the game turns early.",
